    <content:encoded>[caption id="attachment_2055" align="alignleft" width="225"]&lt;a href="https://flyingsummers.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/08/guymon-ok.jpeg"&gt;&lt;img class="size-medium wp-image-2055" src="https://flyingsummers.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/08/guymon-ok.jpeg?w=225" alt="Quick stop, rest and fuel" width="225" height="300" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Quick stop, rest and fuel[/caption]

We weren't able to get out of Albuquerque last night (thunderstorms, night, mountains), but we were up early and out in the morning.

[caption id="attachment_2054" align="alignright" width="225"]&lt;a href="https://flyingsummers.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/08/jack-stack.jpeg"&gt;&lt;img class="size-medium wp-image-2054" src="https://flyingsummers.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/08/jack-stack.jpeg?w=225" alt="Lunch!" width="225" height="300" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Lunch![/caption]

A fuel stop on Guymon, OK made us think of our friend Dean. Now we are in Kansas City where we landed on a flat tire. Everyone is fine and we are enjoying some BBQ.</content:encoded>
